From 31ef28842d38bd9a8d6b792ec33c5f531590db91
Subject: Track previous-frame visibility on ViewVisibility instead of hash sets
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/31ef28842d38bd9a8d6b792ec33c5f531590db91
Date: 2026-07-06T14:56:21+01:00

check_visibility, check_point_light_mesh_visibility and the newly-hidden
marking maintained per-frame EntityHashSets (PreviousVisibleEntities),
inserting and removing every visible entity every frame — ~5-6% of
main-thread time on our CPU-bound wasm workload.

Adapt upstream #22226 (bevy 0.18) to 0.16: ViewVisibility becomes
(current, previous); reset copies current->previous and clears current via
bypass_change_detection; visibility producers use a new SetViewVisibility
trait (set_visible on Mut<ViewVisibility>) that only triggers change
detection on hidden->visible; newly-hidden marking becomes a parallel
component scan. Ports the corrected upstream semantics (the merged #22226
had two bugs fixed later on main), not the PR diff.

Change-detection behavior is bit-exact vs the hashset protocol, so
render-world extraction (Changed<ViewVisibility> filters, RemovedComponents
cleanup) is unaffected. Public API preserved: ViewVisibility::set() and
Deref<Target = bool> kept (boimp relies on both), PreviousVisibleEntities
retained as an always-empty compat shell. Known soft cost: an external
producer using the old guarded set() pattern (boimp's bake visibility)
now triggers spurious re-extraction while a bake camera is active; the
one-line fix there is to use set_visible().

Measured (wasm, Genesis Plaza, fixed viewpoint): visibility-set hash churn
6.2% -> 0.9% of main-thread time; 30 -> ~36fps cumulative with the mesh/
material instance mirror work.

NOTE: THROWAWAY on migration to bevy >= 0.18 — this is upstream #22226's
design and comes for free on rebase; drop this commit, do not port it.
